@page "/null-attribute"
@rendermode @(new InteractiveServerRenderMode(prerender: false))

@*
    Prerendering is off for the reason recorded on FoldParityPage.razor and NullAttributeView.cs: with it
    on, the first HTML response already carries the final attributes, and a first render batch identical to
    that DOM produces no edits, so the client-side renderer this page exists to exercise never runs. The
    spec's first test fetches this URL with no browser involved and asserts the ids are absent, so the claim
    stays true rather than being assumed.

    /null-attribute-prerender is the sibling with prerendering left on, for PrerenderTests, which wants the
    opposite from the same view.
*@
<NullAttributeView />
